On Feb 16, 2013, at 6:03 AM, Saptarshi Guha wrote:

> For some reason, when i install rJava all i get is JRI.jar (which doesn't have REXPJavaReference or JRIEngine ..)
> Am i missing something during install?
> 

No, JRI has only the classes for the low-level engine. REngine is separate layer on top of it. The fact that REngine doesn't ship with JRI is really for historical reasons since REngine was first created with the Rserve back-end and JRI was added later. But you have a very good point that it should really be shipped together.

For now, you'll have to get JRIEngine.jar and REngine.jar from
http://rforge.net/JRI/files/
sorry about that. I'll see if I can add them to the rJava build.

Thanks,
Simon



